        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ನರ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನರ — nara — \"a nerve; a sinew\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವೈದ್ಯರು ಅವನ ಕೈಯ ನರವನ್ನು ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಿದರು. vaidyaru avana kaiya naravannu parīkṣisidaru. The doctor examined the nerve in his arm."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ನರಗಳು, naragaḷu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In everyday talk also a vein; ನರಗಳು, the nerves."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನರ (nara) is native Dravidian: DEDR 2903 lists Kannada nara, naravu, \"sinew, tendon, nerve, vein\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
